-- title:
--   Mennicke's composite step: Q_{m''} lies in [Q_{m''},Q_{m''}]∨ Q_{m'm''}
-- statement:
--   Work in $\mathrm{SL}_2(R)$ with $R = \mathbb{Z}[1/q]$, realised as the localisation `ZAway q` of $\mathbb{Z}$ away from $q$, and for a natural number $m$ write $Q_m =$ [`Ihara.mennickeQ q m`](def/IharaMennickeCarrier.html#L115) for the normal closure in $\mathrm{SL}_2(R)$ of the singleton $\{\,\iota(A)^m\,\}$, where $A = \begin{pmatrix}1&0\\1&1\end{pmatrix}$ is [`Ihara.mennickeA`](def/IharaMennickeCarrier.html#L14) and $\iota =$ [`Ihara.slToAway q`](def/IharaAmalgamMap.html#L12) is the homomorphism $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) \to \mathrm{SL}_2(R)$ induced by the structure map $\mathbb{Z} \to R$. Let $q$ be a nonzero natural number and let $m', m''$ be nonzero natural numbers such that: $m'$ and $m''$ are coprime; each of $m'$, $m''$ and $m'm''$ is coprime to $q$; $m'$ is coprime to $q^2-1$ (truncated subtraction of natural numbers); and $q^2-1$ divides $m''$. The assertion is the inclusion of subgroups of $\mathrm{SL}_2(R)$
--   $$Q_{m''} \;\le\; \bigl[Q_{m''},Q_{m''}\bigr] \;\vee\; Q_{m'm''},$$
--   the right-hand side being the subgroup generated by the commutator subgroup of $Q_{m''}$ together with $Q_{m'm''}$.
--
--   This is Mennicke's step showing that, for admissible splittings $m = m'm''$, the quotient $Q_{m''}/Q_{m'm''}$ is perfect, in the form needed for Ihara's modular group $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}[1/q])$; the proof invokes [`Ihara.mennickeLemma21`](thm.html#Ihara.mennickeLemma21). It feeds the congruence-subgroup statement [`Ihara.mennickeCSP_of_prime`](thm.html#Ihara.mennickeCSP_of_prime) and the membership result [`Ihara.pow_card_mem_mennickeQ_mul`](thm.html#Ihara.pow_card_mem_mennickeQ_mul).
-- source:
